{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BQQCamyZPGXB9njkNdeMN4","type":"tool_result","content":"7680 0.508854\n1c1\n< \"\"\"Most lopsided stretch: one striking local heads/tails excess makes a sequence look designed.\n---\n> \"\"\"Personal side bias on top of most-lopsided-stretch aversion.\n3,9c3,9\n< People notice the single contiguous stretch in which heads most outnumber tails\n< (or vice versa) — the largest local excess, a maximum over sub-sequences, not\n< only unbroken streaks — and that one stretch makes the sequence look less random\n< by a shared weight. This sits on the current best judgement (personal ideal\n< switching rate and sensitivity, personal weights on imbalance and the longest\n< run, shared weights on the final run, mirror symmetry and run-length variety,\n< personal lapse rate).\n---\n> Refinement of `most_lopsided_stretch_aversion`: each sequence's apparent\n> randomness is judged exactly as in that model (personal ideal switching rate and\n> sensitivity, personal weights on imbalance and the longest run, shared weights on\n> the final run, mirror symmetry, run-length variety and the most lopsided stretch,\n> personal lapse rate). The one change: each person has a habitual leaning toward\n> the left or right button (drawn from a population that may lean one way overall)\n> that tips every engaged comparison toward that side by a fixed logit amount.\n157c157,163\n<     p_engaged = pm.math.sigmoid(score_a - score_b)\n---\n>     # Personal response-side bias (positive: leans toward the left button).\n>     mu_side = pm.Normal(\"mu_side\", mu=0.0, sigma=0.5)\n>     sigma_side = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_side\", sigma=0.5)\n>     z_side = pm.Normal(\"z_side\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n>     side = mu_side + sigma_side * z_side\n> \n>     p_engaged = pm.math.sigmoid(score_a - score_b + side[participant_id])\n1c1\n< \"\"\"Most lopsided stretch: one striking local heads/tails excess makes a sequence look designed.\n---\n> \"\"\"Most lopsided stretch with an asymmetric tolerance around the ideal switching rate.\n3,6c3,4\n< People notice the single contiguous stretch in which heads most outnumber tails\n< (or vice versa) — the largest local excess, a maximum over sub-sequences, not\n< only unbroken streaks — and that one stretch makes the sequence look less random\n< by a shared weight. This sits on the current best judgement (personal ideal\n---\n> Refinement of `most_lopsided_stretch_aversion`: one striking local heads/tails\n> excess still makes a sequence look designed, on top of the personal ideal\n9c7,9\n< personal lapse rate).\n---\n> and a personal lapse rate. The one change (grafted from\n> `run_variety_asymmetric_ideal_rate`): switching more often than one's ideal costs\n> only a shared fraction of what the same shortfall in switching costs.\n144a145,148\n>     # Shared fraction of the ideal-rate penalty applied to over-alternation.\n>     log_over = pm.Normal(\"log_over\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n>     over_frac = pm.Deterministic(\"over_frac\", pm.math.exp(log_over))\n> \n155,156c159,164\n<     score_a = -b * pt.sqr(alt_rate_a - theta) - g * imbalance_a - d * maxrun_a - kappa * endrun_a - rho * palin_a + omega * variety_a - eta * lopsided_a\n<     score_b = -b * pt.sqr(alt_rate_b - theta) - g * imbalance_b - d * maxrun_b - kappa * endrun_b - rho * palin_b + omega * variety_b - eta * lopsided_b\n---\n>     def rate_penalty(rate):\n>         dev = rate - theta\n>         return pt.sqr(dev) * pt.switch(dev > 0, over_frac, 1.0)\n> \n>     score_a = -b * rate_penalty(alt_rate_a) - g * imbalance_a - d * maxrun_a - kappa * endrun_a - rho * palin_a + omega * variety_a - eta * lopsided_a\n>     score_b = -b * rate_penalty(alt_rate_b) - g * imbalance_b - d * maxrun_b - kappa * endrun_b - rho * palin_b + omega * variety_b - eta * lopsided_b","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"124ca037-d810-428c-bb62-4b10e0d2f167","uuid":"7bd88043-19af-421c-