{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdL8Mcu7KcY8sFVhshie","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WmF53aA3EthdXFr1qB8t5g","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"M=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop; D=$M/iter_1/candidate_5_repair_1\npython3 - <<'PY'\nM=\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop\"\nsrc=open(M+\"/models/asymmetric_tolerance_lopsided_stretch.py\").read()\ni=src.index('\"\"\"',3)+3\ndoc='''\"\"\"Personal button-side bias on the asymmetric-tolerance lopsided-stretch judgement.\n\nRefinement of `personal_side_bias_lopsided_stretch`: each person has a habitual\nleaning toward the left or right button (drawn from a population that may lean\none way overall) that tips every engaged comparison toward that side by a fixed\nlogit amount, on top of the most-lopsided-stretch judgement (personal ideal\nswitching rate and sensitivity, personal weights on imbalance and the longest\nrun, shared weights on the final run, mirror symmetry, run-length variety and the\nmost lopsided stretch, personal lapse rate). The one change: the asymmetric\ntolerance of `asymmetric_tolerance_lopsided_stretch` is grafted in, so switching\nmore often than one's ideal costs only a shared fraction of what the same\nshortfall costs.\n\"\"\"'''\nsrc=doc+src[i:]\nold=\"    p_engaged = pm.math.sigmoid(score_a - score_b)\"\nassert old in src\nnew='''    # Personal response-side bias (positive: leans toward the left button).\n    mu_side = pm.Normal(\"mu_side\", mu=0.0, sigma=0.5)\n    sigma_side = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_side\", sigma=0.5)\n    z_side = pm.Normal(\"z_side\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    side = mu_side + sigma_side * z_side\n\n    p_engaged = pm.math.sigmoid(score_a - score_b + side[participant_id])'''\nsrc=src.replace(old,new)\nopen(M+\"/iter_1/candidate_5_repair_1/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nPY\necho side_bias_asymmetric_tolerance_stretch > $D/model_name.txt\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md <<'EOF'\nRefinement of `personal_side_bias_lopsided_stretch` (rank 2): each person still has a habitual leaning toward the left or right response button, drawn from a population that may lean left overall, which tips every comparison they make toward that side by a fixed amount, and each sequence is still judged by the most lopsided stretch on top of a personal ideal switching rate and sensitivity, personal weights on imbalance and the longest streak, shared weights on the final streak, mirror symmetry and run-length variety, and a personal guessing rate. The one change is grafting in the incumbent's asymmetric tolerance: switching more often than one's ideal costs only a shared fraction of what the same shortfall in switching costs — so the button leaning (the critique's excess spread of people's left-choice rates) is estimated on top of the best current judgement of randomness rather than on a weaker one.\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses $M/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2634,"cache_read_input_tokens":81996,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2634,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"124ca037-d810-428c-bb62-4b10e0d2f167","uuid":"73ea9d77-899e-46e4-9ceb-3abd044f2047","timestamp":"2026-10-02T11:27:52.415Z","request_id":"req_011CfdL8MDLt2gWmJASWkFSu"}
